<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's 1996/97 harvest was speeding ahead March 28, and was well ahead of the same date last season, the Agriculture Secretariat said in its weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>Maize harvesting was 34.4 percent complete, compared to progress of just 26.9 percent at the same point last season. Sorghum harvesting was 26.2 percent over, compared to 5.6 percent. Soybean harvesting was 3.8 percent over. Sunflower seed yields have been a disappointment. The seeds are light, with too much husk and a lower fat content than last season. Low rainfall and high temperatures was speeding soybean development.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets). Yield in quintals per hectare.</p>
<p> ..........Planting.............Harvest..................Yield</p>
<p> Wheat     6,983  100.0(100.0) 6,694.4  100.0   (n/a)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Maize     3,890  100.0(100.0) 1,204.8   34.4  (26.9)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Soybeans  6,583  100.0(100.0)   254.9    3.8   (1.4)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sunflower 3,075  100.0(100.0) 2,220.6   74.5  (75.6)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Sorghum     778  100.0(100.0)   191.0   26.2   (5.6)    (n/a)</p>
<p> Cotton	952  100.0  (n/a)    62.4    7.7   (6.4)    (n/a)</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
